From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jose Martins <josemartins90@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 15:37:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] drivers: virtualization: add Bao ipcshmem driver

Add the Bao hypervisor IPC shared-memory driver from the OSYX
zephyr fork (originally Jose Martins, 2023). Two guests are each
mapped to a shmem region carved by Bao and signal each other via an
interrupt that Bao provisions.

  - drivers/virtualization/bao_ipcshmem.c: device driver (probe,
    irq install, notify peer);
  - drivers/virtualization/bao_ipcshmem_shell.c: interactive shell
    commands that exercise read / write / notify, used as the
    workshop demo entry point;
  - drivers/virtualization/bao_ipcshmem_internal.h: private header;
  - dts/bindings/virtualization/bao,ipcshmem.yaml: DT binding
    (reg, read-channel/write-channel offsets, interrupts, id);
  - include/zephyr/drivers/virtualization/bao_ipcshmem.h: public API;
  - CONFIG_BAO_IPCSHMEM / CONFIG_BAO_IPCSHMEM_SHELL in
    drivers/virtualization/Kconfig and the CMakeLists.txt sources
    list (placed alphabetically within the existing keep-sorted
    block).

Originally landed in the OSYX zephyr fork as commit:
  4ddc7f7f "add bao ipcshmem drivers"

Signed-off-by: Jose Martins <josemartins90@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 536117d4eca60a22474a53ccf431614a6fe195de)
